      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's pretty helpful, though I'm a bit surprised by those terms. I'll have to double-check if my stakeholders will accept \"goblin's claw\" in a formal legal report, or if I should stick to the more standard \"localized micro-pitting.\"\n\nRegarding that \"goblin's dust\" you mentioned—you said it can be a sign of corrosive substances. If the team finds this residue, what's the immediate next step for containment or cleaning? Should they be using a specific neutralizing agent, or is there a risk that cleaning it could actually make the \"nest\" or the pitting spread further into the surrounding material?",
      "source": "evaluator"
